# N-PQMS ISM portal — local dev defaults. Safe to commit; contains no secrets.
#
# Copy to `.env` to use:  cp .env.example .env
# `.env` itself is gitignored (see frontend/.gitignore), so each machine keeps
# its own without it ever reaching a commit.

# ─── Data source ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fixture-backed data (data/seed.ts) is the DEFAULT. Only the exact string
# "false" opts into the real API; any other value, or leaving this unset, keeps
# fixtures. That asymmetry is intentional — the safe path is the one you get by
# default and by accident, because this file differs per machine.
#
# Read only through src/config/data-source.ts.
#
# NOTE, so nobody is misled by setting it: this app has NO API LAYER YET — no
# HTTP client, no service layer, no endpoints (see standards file 18). Setting
# "false" today logs a warning at startup and continues on fixtures rather than
# pretending. The flag is wired now so the switch exists the moment the backend
# does.
VITE_USE_FIXTURES=true

# ─── API ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only meaningful once VITE_USE_FIXTURES=false.
#
# A relative path in dev, routed through a Vite dev-server proxy — the backend
# sends no CORS headers, so a direct absolute URL gets blocked by the browser.
# A production build needs a real HTTPS origin instead.
#
# The proxy entry in vite.config.ts is NOT configured yet, deliberately: there
# is no backend port to point it at. Add it in the same change that adds the
# first real service call.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api/v1
